  "goodToKnow": "Die Gehirnerschütterung is a concussion, with symptoms such as Kopfschmerzen, Übelkeit (nausea) and Schwindel (dizziness). In the 2014 World Cup final, German player Christoph Kramer played on with a concussion and later couldn't remember the match; he had asked the referee whether this was really the final. Sports federations have since tightened concussion rules. Plural: die Gehirnerschütterungen."
